Translation patch: `src/packets/session_state_change.rs`

Change:
  - `.map(Self)`, `.map(SessionStateChange::Schema)`, `.map(SessionStateChange::TransactionState)` become `match`es.
  - The three loops over system variables move into recursive private helpers: `deserialize_system_variables(buf, vars)` (`while !buf.is_empty() { vars.push(buf.parse_unchecked(())?) }`), `serialize_system_variables(vars, i, buf)` (`for var in vars { var.serialize(buf) }`), and `system_variables_to_owned(&x, i, vars)` for `x.into_iter().map(SystemVariable::into_owned).collect()`, which uses a new private `SystemVariable::to_owned_static(&self)` building `RawBytes::new(bytes.to_vec())` for the name and the value.
  - `is_tracked.as_bytes() == b"1"` becomes `is_tracked.as_bytes() == &b"1"[..]`.
Why: Aeneas fails on constructors used as values (patch 09) and on loops over a `Vec` whose elements hold borrows ("Nested borrows", "Could not match the contexts", "loan and borrow in the same region"); `PartialEq<[u8; N]> for [u8]` is not modelled.
Behaviour: Identical results: the recursion visits the same elements in the same order with the same early `Err` returns; `to_owned_static` gives the same value as `into_owned`: `as_bytes()` is the whole buffer because `LenEnc::MAX_LEN = usize::MAX` (no truncation), so both are an owned copy of the same bytes (it copies an already-owned buffer instead of moving it, so the `Vec`'s capacity can differ, which is not part of the value); comparing with the array or the full slice of it is the same comparison. The recursion uses stack proportional to the number of system variables.

